= Information theory — Technical =

== Entropy ==
For discrete X:

<pre>
H(X) = -Σ_x p(x) log p(x)
</pre>

== Conditional entropy ==
<pre>
H(X|Y) = H(X,Y) - H(Y)
</pre>

== Mutual information ==
<pre>
I(X;Y) = H(X) + H(Y) - H(X,Y)
       = D_KL(P_XY || P_X P_Y)
</pre>

Mutual information is zero exactly when X and Y are independent under the usual discrete/continuous measure assumptions.

== Coding limits ==
Source coding relates expected code length to entropy.

Channel coding relates reliable transmission rate to channel capacity.

Rate–distortion theory studies lossy compression when controlled distortion is permitted.

